{"project": "integer-pricing", "file": "pricing.py", "requirements": "Inputs are integers; money is non-negative cents. line_total_cents(unit_cents,quantity,discount_pct): unit_cents and quantity >=0, discount_pct in 0..100; apply percentage discount to the whole line and floor once to integer cents. shipping_cents(subtotal_cents): reject negatives, free shipping for subtotal >=5000, otherwise 599. refund_cents(paid_cents,returned_qty,total_qty): paid_cents>=0, total_qty>0, 0<=returned_qty<=total_qty; prorate the whole paid amount and floor once. Invalid values must raise ValueError. Keep exactly these three signatures. No imports, attributes, subscripts, loops, decorators or arbitrary calls; only integer arithmetic, comparisons, if/return, and ValueError/min/max are supported.", "source": "def line_total_cents(unit_cents, quantity, discount_pct):
